## Files written
- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` — added section **7. FOLLOW ORDER** exporting `followedBeforeWrite(events, command)`; renumbered the following section headers to 8/9/10. No other file touched.

What it does: strips the leading slash and a `:auto|:confirm|:autopilot|:unattended` suffix, then finds the first `write` position. It is true when a `read` (or `skill`) event names the command's document before that boundary, either as `.skilled/commands/<ns>/<name>.md`, a runtime mirror (`.claude/...`, flat `.cursor/commands/<ns>-<name>.md`), or a skill event naming `<ns>:<name>`. A read of the command's `-confirm.yaml`/`.yml` asset at or after the first write makes it false. Whether a command ships a confirm workflow is not read from disk, so a checkout file cannot turn a clean transcript into a failure; a run that wrote nothing is decided by its document read alone. Paths match on the `commands/...` tail so every runtime root works without a per-runtime path table.

